# Lesson numbers follow teaching order

Readers see **1, 2, 3...** in sidebar order. Never jump (80 then 409) and never duplicate.

`id="section-N"`, `data-section="N"`, `.lesson-card__marker`, and TOC `href="#section-N"` must match.

## How to pick the next number

Teaching order is the `[data-include]` list in `index.html` (same as the sidebar).

1. **Add at the end** of that list: continue from the last lesson on the site plus 1. No shift.
2. **Insert in the middle**: first lesson of the new chapter is **last lesson of the previous chapter in that list, plus 1**. Then **shift every later chapter up** by the number of new lessons.
3. Do this even for bonus blocks (Python, NumPy, Pandas). Do not continue from the latest published 100 day if that day sits later in the course.

## Example

Day 12 ends at 80. Python is next on the site, so Python starts at 81. NumPy, Pandas, Day 13, and later all move up.

If you later insert a chapter between Day 20 and Day 21, start from Day 20's last lesson plus 1, then shift Day 21 onward.

## Update every place

- Day file: `id`, `data-section`, `.lesson-card__marker`
- `index.html` sidebar TOC links
- Any `href="#section-N"` inside lessons
- Later chapters after a middle insert (all of the above)

Do **not** restart at 1 inside a chapter. Do **not** leave later chapters on old numbers.

After includes load, `script.js` also numbers cards in page order so the badge cannot jump even if a day file still has an old number. Still keep the HTML numbers in teaching order so files, TOC, and links stay aligned.
